  "post": {
    "caption": "Ratnapura's gem pits hold ancient hippo fossils. The Sri Lankan town southeast of Colombo is known for gems, and miners there dig pits by hand down to gem gravel called illam, then wash it in woven baskets. Sri Lanka was long known as Ratna Dweepa, or Gem Island. Ptolemy mentioned its sapphires in the second century, and Marco Polo wrote about them around 1300. Ratnapura means city of gems.",
